Subject: Urgent: min.per.group for multiple groups
Message-ID: <0-G5QvXGQc4.mHccG3GjAQAJ@methylkit-discussion.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/methylkit_discussion/c/0-G5QvXGQc4/m/mHccG3GjAQAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Hi,

I am wondering how the min.per.group works when I have 2 groups, one with treatment=0, and the other with treatment=1.

Say I have 12 samples with treatment=0, and 3 samples with treatment=1.  If I want to get minimum 11 out of the 12 samples with treatment=0 & all the 3 treatment=1 samples, should I use min.per.group=c(3L, 11L) or c(11L, 3L)?

Thank you very much,
Rajat

From u38c56d0e82a34280 at groups.google.com  Fri Jul 22 02:20:05 2016
From: u38c56d0e82a34280 at groups.google.com (Dhruva Chandramohan)
Date: Fri, 22 Jul 2016 02:20:05 +0000
Subject: Re: [methylkit_discussion] Urgent: min.per.group for multiple groups
Message-ID: <0-G5QvXGQc4.r1504C2mAQAJ@methylkit-discussion.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <0-G5QvXGQc4.mHccG3GjAQAJ@methylkit-discussion.groups.google.com>
References: <0-G5QvXGQc4.mHccG3GjAQAJ@methylkit-discussion.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/methylkit_discussion/c/0-G5QvXGQc4/m/r1504C2mAQAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The current functionality (based on the source code here <https://github.com/al2na/methylKit/blob/master/R/backbone.R> , about halfway down) expects a single integer to be used for both groups, so it won't quite do what you want. One quasi-solution would be to use the reorganize function to temporarily assign the samples to a single group, to at least ensure coverage over most of the data.

If you really want to try with unequal groups and need it quickly, you can try copying the code and making your own custom version of the unite function by tweaking this section to make min.per.group a vector and indexing into it:

for(i in unique(object@treatment) ){
my.ind=coverage.ind[object@treatment==i]
ldat = !is.na <http://is.na>(df[,my.ind,with=FALSE])
if( is.null(dim(ldat)) ){ # if there is only one dimension
df=df[ldat>=min.per.group,]
}else{
df=df[rowSums(ldat)>=min.per.group,]
}
}

